        // The mutant also won't revert, but will return a different boolean for at least one input.
        // We assert a general fact that holds for the reference for all inputs: calling supportsInterface
        // does not revert (ok == true). The mutant also won't revert, so this assertion won't distinguish.
        // To produce a failing case on the mutant, we assert that if interfaceId equals IERC165's id,
